{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
  "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SHELDON E. RICHIE, ESQ., Austin, Texas; on behalf of Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "NEAL K. KATYAL, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is it your position that all of the actions of the board, including those taken by the regional offices and by the general counsel and by everybody else, is inoperative once -- once the membership falls below three?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But here the court of appeals said that the Act does two things. First, it said that the full board can delegate full powers to any three-member group. That was step one, and that was done here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You should -- you should have a very direct answer to this question. Were you finished, because I don't want to interrupt that train of thought?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Richie",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RICHIE: Justice Breyer, the legislative history I think is -- there is no legislative history on what happens when the board falls below two members. But it is clear that from 1935 to 1947, the board was made up of three members, and the statute clearly said under the Wagner Act two members could be a quorum of a three-member board."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The amicus says that the members of the board not serving on a panel are given the opportunity to review draft decisions, thus no case will issue unless it reflects the majority opinion of the full board."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, faced with a vacancy crisis, the board validly delegated its powers in December 2007 to a three-member panel, and Petitioners have never contested otherwise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the language of the quorum provision, \"quorum\" meaning a number sufficient to transact business, is the most relevant language, and that suggests that two is enough so long as you have that initial delegation to a group of three and then one member drops off."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it is a long-established principle that principal/agent relationships, which we don't think necessarily apply to this case, but even did you -- even were you to disagree, as the premise of your question suggested, that government delegations survive the loss of that principal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is your point that official acts done stay in effect even though the official is gone, until the official's successor in office is appointed and that successor can remand the instruction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that, for example, when an attorney general designates their power to -- the wiretap authority to a subordinate, an assistant attorney general, and then that attorney general leaves office, that wiretap authority nonetheless continues in the subordinate until it is revoked by a successor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But hasn't the situation that has prevailed now for some time changed the -- the decision-making process of the board in at least two important ways? First, there isn't any opportunity for full board review of cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think that Congress had before it a well -- it was well-known that over 460 times the board had decided cases with only two members, with the third being vacant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if -- if the choice is shutting down or going with two, the board made the choice in this circumstance to go with more."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1457",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
